# 64-bit build (milestone 12, way A): fixed byte offsets into structures whose
# members move on LP64 (found with port/tools/m12/raw_offset_check.py). Each
# offset becomes RE4_OFS(T, member, gc) (re4_whole_prelude.h): the member's
# offset, checked against the GameCube value on ILP32 at compile time, so the
# 32-bit builds keep the same addresses.
# - em2d.cpp, sce_com.cpp, r100.cpp, r103.cpp: player / enemy members
#   (cPlayer dmg.m_PosFrom, pos, ang; cEm subArc).
# - em32.cpp, r307.cpp, r318.cpp: members of the room and enemy works.
# - t_camera.cpp, t_camera_draw.cpp: the camera tool's pad words (TC_ON,
#   TC_TRG, TC_REP) and pad copies; t_esp.cpp: the effect tool's numeric
#   widgets (FSTORE_AT on LP64 through max / min / unit, nameTbl / nameNum).
# - ss_pzzl.cpp (also 32 bit): CMES_FLAGS / CMES_RESULT read message 1's
#   state and selection at MWCC's offsets (vptr behind the fields); with the
#   port's layout (vptr first) they read be_flag and a byte of m_selTbl. Now
#   through MessageControl::GetMesStatus / GetSelectMessage.
--- a/src/Sscrn/ss_pzzl.cpp
